# Run artefacts produced inside the pipeline directory. The code is versioned;
# the output of running it is not.

# SLURM job output. run_all_v2.sh creates this directory, because
# "#SBATCH --output=slurm_logs/..." silently loses output if it does not exist
# and git cannot track an empty directory.
slurm_logs/

# Scratch / working data written during a run.
data/

# Generated, not source: run_all_v2.sh truncates and rebuilds this on every run by
# scanning GENOMES/*/*/*/metadata.yaml for "active: true". Tracking it means every
# run shows a spurious diff, and a run against a wrong or unmounted GENOMES path
# silently empties the tracked copy.
#
# Nothing READS this any more -- it is a human-readable snapshot of "what is active
# right now". The SLURM array indexes into runs/genesets.<id>.tsv instead, so that a
# status check (or a second submission) cannot renumber a running array's task list.
active_genesets.tsv

# Per-run frozen copies of the task list, one per submission. Kept after the run so a
# finished array can still be matched to exactly the genesets it was given.
runs/

# check_status.sh's own listing. Separate from the above on purpose: it used to share
# active_genesets.tsv with run_all_v2.sh and truncated it out from under live jobs.
status_genesets.tsv
